Game-playing agents. Random, greedy and MCTS (Monte Carlo Tree Search) agents. The determinize method means MCTS samples guesses at the opponent’s hidden hand, which is a standard technique for games with hidden information.
Simulation. A simulator runs thousands of games, with balance reports that include confidence intervals.
Statistical testing. The card swap test, seat advantage check and skill-versus-luck check are all controlled experiments. They compare win rates between decks that differ in only one thing.
Planned optimization methods. Hill climbing, simulated annealing or a genetic algorithm to tune the parameters.
